!!! nil-web, demonstrated.
!!!
!!! A whole request/response cycle with no socket in it: a request arrives as
!!! text, the guards run, the router picks a handler, the handler builds a
!!! response from a template, the finishers add their headers, and the
!!! response is rendered back to text. That is the entire framework, and it is
!!! deliberately the entire framework — whatever ends up accepting connections
!!! calls `answer` with what it read and writes back what it gets.
!!!
!!! The dispatch below is the shape every application using this takes: a
!!! route table of names, and one `switch` that turns a name into a call.
!!! Matrix has no capturing closures and cannot hold a callable in an array,
!!! so the name is the indirection. See the router for the long version.

book nilweb.main

read nil.std.text
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read nil.std.core
read everything from nilweb.http.method
read everything from nilweb.http.status
read everything from nilweb.http.headers
read everything from nilweb.http.request
read everything from nilweb.http.response
read everything from nilweb.http.uri
read everything from nilweb.routing.router
read everything from nilweb.template.context
read everything from nilweb.template.render
read everything from nilweb.session.session
read everything from nilweb.static.files
read nil.std.text.string_utils
read everything from nilweb.middleware.chain
read everything from nilweb.server.engine
read everything from nilweb.time.clock
read everything from nilweb.log.access
read everything from nilweb.config.settings
read nil.std.system.environment


!!! The running configuration, and the site a request is being answered for.
!!!
!!! Book globals rather than arguments threaded through every handler. The
!!! alternative is one more parameter on `answer-parsed`, `page-shell`,
!!! `rendered-page` and each page, which is five signatures changed so that
!!! one of them can read a path. A single-threaded server has one active
!!! request at a time, so there is nothing here for a second one to race with
!!! — and if that ever stops being true, this is the thing that has to change.
public variable active-settings is default-settings with nothing
public variable active-site is build site with host being "", template-root being "web",
    public-root being "web/public", index-page being ""

constant site-name as text is "nil-web"


!!! --- The application's route table.

demo-routes returns array of route begin paragraph
    variable routes is no-routes with nothing
    set routes to get-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/", handler being "home"
    set routes to get-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/posts", handler being "posts"
    set routes to get-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/hello/:name", handler being "hello"
    set routes to get-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/search", handler being "search"
    set routes to get-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/assets/*rest", handler being "asset"
    set routes to post-route with routes being routes, pattern being "/users", handler being "create-user"
    give routes
end paragraph


!!! --- What runs around every handler.

demo-chain returns chain begin paragraph
    variable built is new-chain with nothing
    set built to with-guard with one-chain being built, kind being "require-host", setting being ""
    set built to with-guard with one-chain being built, kind being "body-limit", setting being "65536"
    set built to with-finisher with one-chain being built, kind being "security-headers", setting being ""
    set built to with-finisher with one-chain being built, kind being "server-name", setting being "nil-web"
    give built
end paragraph


!!! --- One request in, one response out. This is what a transport calls.

public answer receives raw as text returns text begin paragraph
    give answer-parsed with request being (parse-request with raw being raw)
end paragraph


!!! --- The same, for a caller that has already parsed.
!!!
!!! The serving loop needs the parsed request anyway, for the access log. When
!!! `answer` took only text, the loop parsed once for the log and `answer`
!!! parsed again for the response, and that second parse cost a third of the
!!! throughput. Measured, not guessed: 422 req/s became 270.

public answer-parsed receives request as http-request returns text begin paragraph
    !!! Which site answers, decided once per request from the Host header. A
    !!! Host nothing is configured for is refused rather than served from
    !!! whichever site happens to be first, because that is how one tenant
    !!! ends up reading another's pages.
    when request.well-formed then
        set nilweb.main::active-site to site-for with held-settings being nilweb.main::active-settings,
            host-header being (host-of with request being request)
        when (nilweb.main::active-site).template-root equals "" then
            give render-response with response being (error-response with code being status-not-found,
                explanation being "No site is configured for that host"), verb being request.verb
        end when
    end when
    when not request.well-formed then
        give render-for-get with response being
            (error-response with code being status-bad-request, explanation being request.complaint)
    end when

    value around is demo-chain with nothing
    value checked is run-guards with one-chain being around, request being request
    when checked.stopped then
        give render-response with response being (run-finishers with one-chain being around,
            response being checked.response), verb being request.verb
    end when

    value found is match-route with routes being (demo-routes with nothing),
        verb being request.verb, path being request.path

    value answered is when found.matched
        give (run-handler with name being found.handler, request being request, found being found)
        otherwise give (when found.path-matched
            give (method-not-allowed-response with allowed being found.allowed)
            otherwise give (not-found-response with path being request.path)
        end when)
    end when

    give render-response with response being (run-finishers with one-chain being around, response being answered),
        verb being request.verb
end paragraph


!!! --- The one switch an application owns. A name with no case here is a
!!! wiring mistake, and it answers 500 saying which name, rather than
!!! silently answering 404 as though the route had never been declared.

run-handler receives name as text, request as http-request, found as route-result
    returns http-response begin paragraph
    give switch name
        case "home" then
            stop switching with (home-page with request being request)
        case "posts" then
            stop switching with (posts-page with request being request)
        case "hello" then
            stop switching with (hello-page with found being found)
        case "search" then
            stop switching with (search-page with request being request)
        case "asset" then
            stop switching with (asset-file with request being request, found being found)
        case "create-user" then
            stop switching with (create-user with request being request)
        otherwise
            stop switching with (error-response with code being status-internal-error,
                explanation being "No handler is wired for the name " plus quote plus name plus quote)
    end switch
end paragraph


!!! --- The data every page needs: who is reading, and what to call the site.

page-shell receives request as http-request, title as text returns render-context begin paragraph
    variable page-data is empty-context with nothing
    set page-data to with-value with page-data being page-data, name being "site", content being site-name
    set page-data to with-value with page-data being page-data, name being "title", content being title
    value who is session-id-of with request being request
    set page-data to with-flag with page-data being page-data, name being "signed-in", held being not (who equals "")
    set page-data to with-value with page-data being page-data, name being "who", content being who
    give page-data
end paragraph


!!! --- Render a template, or say plainly that it could not be rendered.
!!!
!!! A template fault is a 500 with its complaint, not a half-page. A page that
!!! renders its first half and then stops is the hardest kind of bug to see.

rendered-page receives name as text, page-data as render-context returns http-response begin paragraph
    value outcome is render-file with name being name, page-data being page-data,
        root being (nilweb.main::active-site).template-root
    when not outcome.rendered then
        give error-response with code being status-internal-error,
            explanation being "Template " plus name plus ": " plus outcome.complaint
    end when
    give html-response with body being outcome.text-out
end paragraph


home-page receives request as http-request returns http-response begin paragraph
    variable page-data is page-shell with request being request, title being "Home"
    set page-data to with-value with page-data being page-data, name being "heading", content being "nil-web"
    give rendered-page with name being "home.nilhtml", page-data being page-data
end paragraph


posts-page receives request as http-request returns http-response begin paragraph
    variable page-data is page-shell with request being request, title being "Posts"
    variable rows is no-rows with nothing
    set rows to add-row with rows being rows, one-row being (post-row with title being "Matrix has no closures",
        slug being "no-closures")
    set rows to add-row with rows being rows, one-row being (post-row with title being "Why there is no server yet",
        slug being "no-server")
    set page-data to with-rows with page-data being page-data, name being "posts", rows being rows
    set page-data to with-flag with page-data being page-data, name being "any", held being (the length of rows) is greater than 0
    give rendered-page with name being "posts.nilhtml", page-data being page-data
end paragraph


post-row receives title as text, slug as text returns row begin paragraph
    give row-with with one-row being (row-with with one-row being (new-row with nothing),
        name being "title", content being title), name being "slug", content being slug
end paragraph


hello-page receives found as route-result returns http-response begin paragraph
    value who is capture-of with result being found, name being "name"
    give html-response with body being "<h1>Hello, " plus (escape-html with raw being who) plus "</h1>" plus newline
end paragraph


search-page receives request as http-request returns http-response begin paragraph
    value term is query-of with request being request, name being "q"
    when term equals "" then
        give error-response with code being status-bad-request, explanation being "Pass a search term as ?q="
    end when
    give text-response with body being "Searching for: " plus term plus newline
end paragraph


!!! Through serve-static, so an asset gets an ETag, answers a revalidation
!!! with 304, and honours a Range request. A browser that already has the
!!! stylesheet then sends a conditional request and gets a few dozen bytes
!!! back instead of the file.
asset-file receives request as http-request, found as route-result returns http-response begin paragraph
    value rest is capture-of with result being found, name being "rest"
    give serve-static with root being (nilweb.main::active-site).public-root,
        path being "assets/" plus rest, request being request, seconds being 3600
end paragraph


create-user receives request as http-request returns http-response begin paragraph
    when not (is-form-encoded with request being request) then
        give error-response with code being status-unsupported-media-type,
            explanation being "Send application/x-www-form-urlencoded"
    end when
    value name is form-of with request being request, name being "name"
    when name equals "" then
        give error-response with code being status-unprocessable, explanation being "A user needs a name"
    end when
    give redirect-response with location being "/hello/" plus (encode-component with raw being name)
end paragraph


!!! --- A request as it would arrive, for the demonstration below.

wire-request receives line as text, fields as text, body as text returns text begin paragraph
    !!! Two CRLFs after the fields, not one: the blank line is what ends the
    !!! header section, and a message with only one is a message whose body is
    !!! read as another header.
    give line plus (crlf with nothing) plus fields plus (crlf with nothing) plus (crlf with nothing) plus body
end paragraph


show receives title as text, raw as text returns nothing begin paragraph
    say ""
    say "=== " plus title
    say answer with raw being raw
    give nothing
end paragraph


!!! --- Serve for real.
!!!
!!! An event loop: poll says which sockets can be acted on, the engine frames
!!! whole requests out of whatever arrived, and this loop answers them one at a
!!! time. Many connections are open at once; none of them can hold up another
!!! by sending slowly, reading slowly, or stopping halfway.
!!!
!!! The loop owns no routing. It takes a framed request, hands the text to
!!! `answer`, and hands the result back to the engine — the same `answer` the
!!! demonstration calls with a fixture, so what is served is what is tested.

!!! How many connections may be open at once. Every one holds its accumulated
!!! request, so this is a memory ceiling as much as a load one.
constant connection-ceiling as number is 1024

!!! How long a pass waits when nothing is happening. Short enough that the
!!! idle sweep runs promptly, long enough that an idle server is idle.
constant pass-timeout-ms as number is 1000

serve receives held-settings as settings returns number begin paragraph
    set nilweb.main::active-settings to held-settings
    value host is held-settings.host
    value port is held-settings.port
    variable server is start-engine with host being host, port being port,
        limit being held-settings.connection-limit
    when not server.live then
        say "nil-web could not listen: " plus server.complaint
        give 1
    end when
    when held-settings.share-port then
        value sharing is share-port with server being server
        when not sharing then
            say "nil-web could not share the port; running alone."
        end when
    end when

    !!! Frozen while serving: a template does not change under a running
    !!! server, and frozen means a page costs no filesystem call at all.
    evaluate freeze-cache with frozen being not held-settings.reload-templates

    evaluate log-to with access-file being held-settings.access-log,
        error-file being held-settings.error-log
    when not (held-settings.access-log equals "") then
        say "access log: " plus held-settings.access-log
    end when
    when not (held-settings.error-log equals "") then
        say "error log: " plus held-settings.error-log
    end when
    say "nil-web listening on " plus (address-text with host being host, port being port)
    say (((the length of held-settings.sites) becomes text)) plus " site(s) configured."
    say "Ctrl-C to stop."

    repeat forever
        value ready is pump with server being server, timeout being pass-timeout-ms
        when ready.found then
            value at-ms is now in milliseconds
            !!! Parsed once. `answer-parsed` takes it from here rather than
            !!! parsing the same bytes a second time for the response.
            value request is parse-request with raw being ready.request
            value reply-text is answer-parsed with request being request
            when request.well-formed then
                evaluate record-request with client being ready.peer, request being request,
                    code being (status-in with response-text being reply-text),
                    bytes being (body-length-in with response-text being reply-text), at-ms being at-ms
            end when
            when not request.well-formed then
                evaluate record-malformed with client being ready.peer,
                    code being (status-in with response-text being reply-text), at-ms being at-ms
            end when
            evaluate reply with server being server, handle being ready.handle,
                response being (with-connection-header with response-text being reply-text,
                    keeping being ready.keep-alive),
                keep-open being ready.keep-alive
        end when
        when not ready.found then
            !!! Nothing framed this pass. Close whatever has stopped making
            !!! progress: a connection that said nothing, one sending a request
            !!! a byte at a time, or one idle between keep-alive requests. Then
            !!! write the log, because an idle pass is the one moment when
            !!! three syscalls cost nobody any latency.
            evaluate sweep-idle with server being server
            evaluate flush-now with nothing
            when not (server.complaint equals "") then
                evaluate record-error with severity being "warn", message being server.complaint,
                    at-ms being (now in milliseconds)
                say "loop: " plus server.complaint
                set server.complaint to ""
            end when
        end when
    end repeat
    evaluate stop-engine with server being server
    give 0
end paragraph


!!! --- The status a rendered response carries, read back off the text.
!!!
!!! The loop holds the response as text because that is what goes on the
!!! wire, and the log wants the status and the body length. Read back rather
!!! than threaded through `answer`, which would mean every handler returning a
!!! pair so that one line of logging could have a number.

status-in receives response-text as text returns number begin paragraph
    value space is nil.std.text::index_of with s being response-text, needle being " "
    when space is less than 0 then
        give 0
    end when
    value three is nil.std.text::substring with s being response-text, start being space plus 1, length being 3
    give digits-of with digits being three
end paragraph


body-length-in receives response-text as text returns number begin paragraph
    value marker is (crlf with nothing) plus (crlf with nothing)
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being response-text, needle being marker
    when cut is less than 0 then
        give 0
    end when
    value starts is cut plus 4
    give (nil.std.text::length with s being response-text) minus starts
end paragraph


!!! --- The configuration actually used: the file, then the environment.
!!!
!!! The file is the record of intent and belongs in version control. The
!!! environment overrides it, because a container or a test run needs to
!!! change one value without editing a file it does not own — and because that
!!! is the order every other server does it in, so nobody has to find out.

chosen-settings returns settings begin paragraph
    value named is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_CONFIG"
    value path is when named equals ""
        give (when nil.std.io::exists with path being "nil.web.nildata" give "nil.web.nildata" otherwise give "" end when)
        otherwise give named
    end when

    variable held is load-settings with path being path
    when not held.loaded then
        !!! Said and then carried on with defaults. Refusing to start would
        !!! be defensible; what is not defensible is starting while silently
        !!! ignoring a file somebody wrote.
        say "nil-web: ignoring the configuration file -- " plus held.complaint
    end when
    when not (path equals "") and held.loaded then
        say "configuration: " plus path
    end when

    value host-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_HOST"
    value port-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_PORT"
    value access-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_ACCESS_LOG"
    value error-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_ERROR_LOG"
    value share-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_SHARE_PORT"
    value reload-override is environment-text with name being "NILWEB_RELOAD"

    value stated-port is digits-of with digits being port-override
    give build settings with
        host being (when host-override equals "" give held.host otherwise give host-override end when),
        port being (when stated-port is at least 1 give stated-port otherwise give held.port end when),
        connection-limit being held.connection-limit,
        access-log being (when access-override equals "" give held.access-log otherwise give access-override end when),
        error-log being (when error-override equals "" give held.error-log otherwise give error-override end when),
        share-port being (held.share-port or not (share-override equals "")),
        reload-templates being (held.reload-templates or not (reload-override equals "")),
        sites being held.sites,
        loaded being held.loaded,
        complaint being held.complaint
end paragraph


environment-text receives name as text returns text begin paragraph
    value stated is nil.std.system::get_environment_variable with name being name
    consider stated
        when Option.Some holding text-held then give text-held
        otherwise give ""
    end consider
end paragraph


!!! --- Tell the client what is happening to its connection.
!!!
!!! A keep-alive response must say so, and a response that ends the
!!! connection must say that too: a client left to guess will guess, and a
!!! client that guesses wrong either hangs waiting for a closed socket or
!!! sends its next request into one.
!!!
!!! Inserted after the status line rather than built into the response record,
!!! because whether the connection is kept is the loop's decision and not the
!!! handler's.

with-connection-header receives response-text as text, keeping as boolean returns text begin paragraph
    value marker is crlf with nothing
    value cut is nil.std.text::index_of with s being response-text, needle being marker
    when cut is less than 0 then
        give response-text
    end when
    value line-end is cut plus (nil.std.text::length with s being marker)
    value status-line is nil.std.text::substring with s being response-text, start being 0, length being line-end
    value rest is nil.std.text::substring with s being response-text, start being line-end,
        length being (nil.std.text::length with s being response-text) minus line-end
    value stated is when keeping give "Connection: keep-alive" otherwise give "Connection: close" end when
    give status-line plus stated plus marker plus rest
end paragraph


digits-of receives digits as text returns number begin paragraph
    value width is nil.std.text::length with s being digits
    when width is less than 1 or width is greater than 5 then
        give 0
    end when
    variable total as number is 0
    variable index as number is 0
    repeat while index is less than width
        value code is nil.std.text::byte_at with s being digits, index being index
        when code is less than 48 or code is greater than 57 then
            give 0
        end when
        set total to (total times 10) plus (code minus 48)
        set index to index plus 1
    end repeat
    give total
end paragraph


main returns number begin paragraph
    !!! With NILWEB_SERVE set, this is a server. Without it, it prints the
    !!! same requests through the same `answer`, which is what makes the
    !!! demonstration a demonstration of the thing that actually serves.
    value serving is nil.std.system::get_environment_variable with name being "NILWEB_SERVE"
    consider serving
        when Option.Some holding wanted then begin block
            when not (wanted equals "") then
                give serve with held-settings being (chosen-settings with nothing)
            end when
        end block
        otherwise say ""
    end consider

    say "nil-web demonstration: requests in, responses out."
    say "Set NILWEB_SERVE=1 to serve. Configuration: nil.web.nildata, or NILWEB_CONFIG."

    evaluate show with title being "GET / (template, layout, partial)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET / HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "GET /posts (a loop over rows)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET /posts HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "GET /assets/app.css (a static file)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET /assets/app.css HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "GET /assets/../../outside (traversal, refused)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET /assets/../../nil.project.nildata HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "GET /hello/<script> (escaping)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET /hello/%3Cscript%3E HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "POST /users (form, then redirect)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "POST /users HTTP/1.1",
            fields being "Host: localhost" plus (crlf with nothing) plus "Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded",
            body being "name=Ada+Lovelace")
    evaluate show with title being "GET / with no Host (guard stops it)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET / HTTP/1.1", fields being "Accept: text/html", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "DELETE /users (wrong method)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "DELETE /users HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    evaluate show with title being "GET /nowhere (no route)",
        raw being (wire-request with line being "GET /nowhere HTTP/1.1", fields being "Host: localhost", body being "")
    give 0
end paragraph
